            "Jefe de planta.": "Floor boss.",
            "JEFE EXTRA": "EXTRA BOSS",
            "JEFE EXTRA: BOTÓN MORADO · O LA TRAMPILLA": "EXTRA BOSS: PURPLE BUTTON · OR THE TRAPDOOR",
            Jefes: "Bosses",
            "Jefes (planta 10 / 20 / 30)": "Bosses (floor 10 / 20 / 30)",
            "Jefes de planta, mega jefes y Mewtwo Acorazado": "Floor bosses, mega bosses and Armored Mewtwo",
            "Jefes equilibrados uno a uno (medido con cientos de combates simulados): en cada planta, los combates duran parecido y pegan parecido. Más suaves: Muk (ya no se eterniza), Gengar, Dusknoir, Spiritomb, Magmortar, Arcanine, Steelix, Venomoth, Vileplume, Tyranitar, Aerodactyl y Metagross. Más duros: Golem (ahora embiste de verdad), Weezing, Pinsir, Butterfree, Marowak, Houndoom, Electivire, Onix (en el modo clásico), Gyarados y Dragonite. La Liga Añil no cambia.": "Bosses balanced one by one (measured with hundreds of simulated fights): on each floor, fights last about as long and hit about as hard. Easier: Muk (no longer drags on), Gengar, Dusknoir, Spiritomb, Magmortar, Arcanine, Steelix, Venomoth, Vileplume, Tyranitar, Aerodactyl and Metagross. Harder: Golem (now it really charges), Weezing, Pinsir, Butterfree, Marowak, Houndoom, Electivire, Onix (in Classic mode), Gyarados and Dragonite. The Indigo League doesn't change.",
            "Jefes más justos y antitrampas": "Fairer bosses and anti-cheat",
            "Jefes que se adaptan a ti": "Bosses that adapt to you",
            "Jirachi concede un deseo: objetos sagrados gratis (uno por jugador) y, a veces, un corazón de alma. Sustituye a la sala Distorsión.": "Jirachi grants a wish: free holy items (one per player) and sometimes a soul heart. Replaces the Distortion Room.",
